angement: would need biopsy confirmation of vasculitic pattern", "Endocrine Emergency with Cutaneous Involvement: hyperglycemia alone doesn't establish endocrine crisis"], "alarm_features": ["Markedly elevated blood glucose (>500 mg/dL) indicating severe hyperglycemia", "Multisystem involvement (skin, GI, constitutional symptoms) in 1 week"]}, "branches": {"B1": {"id": "B1", "label": "Endocrine Tumor with Hyperglycemia and Cutaneous Manifestations", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "live", "prior": 0.33366206989709746, "posterior": 0.3336620552813572, "danger": 0.8, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": ["Reactive neutrophilic dermatosis patterns (B4) are moderately supported by the rash's morphology."], "evidence_against": ["The subacute 1-week course weakens the case for endocrine tumors (B1) due to their typical chronic progression, but only slightly."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.7, "interrupt_relevance": 0.8, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism", "representative_diseases": []}, "B2": {"id": "B2", "label": "Insulin Resistance with Systemic and Cutaneous Involvement", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "live", "prior": 0.3455080605443317, "posterior": 0.3455080454096894, "danger": 0.5, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": ["Reactive neutrophilic dermatosis patterns (B4) are moderately supported by the rash's morphology."], "evidence_against": ["Painful rash does not definitively contradict insulin resistance (B2), but adds complexity that weakens its case."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 1.5, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.6, "interrupt_relevance": 0.4, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism", "representative_diseases": []}, "B3": {"id": "B3", "label": "Bet